 r"I am writing to apply for the Analytics Engineer role in the Food Discovery Algorithms team at Just Eat Takeaway.com in Bristol. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have built reliable datasets in SQL and Python, checked their quality, and used them to power models and experiments.",

 r"What attracts me most to this role is that the work has a visible end point: customers finding the restaurants and dishes they will love, because the data behind the ranking models is clean and trustworthy. The posting describes building well-documented ETL datasets for training models and evaluating features, and working closely with data scientists, product and engineering, which is exactly the part of data work I enjoy most. I like taking an unclear question, understanding what the people who own it need, and turning it into something that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I query large merchant and transaction tables in SQL and Python, an e-commerce marketplace much like yours, and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. A large part of the work is agreeing one definition of each metric and checking the data behind it before anyone acts on it. When my supervisor asked me to configure a merchant campaign by hand, I used Claude Code to build an AI agent with a validation step to check its accuracy, which cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing AI product for a pharmaceutical client. I built a Python pipeline that scored more than 2,400 model responses against a 246-question benchmark the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and designed blinded A/B tests to measure whether a new knowledge-graph feature genuinely improved answer quality. I also turned 4,800 free-text patient threads into structured data, which taught me how much of good analysis depends on handling messy and missing data carefully.",

 r"My MSc dissertation used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants, where I engineered features across multiple time points and compared logistic regression with three tree ensembles, checking calibration as well as accuracy. I would bring Just Eat Takeaway.com strong SQL and Python, a statistical mindset, experience with experimentation and data quality, and a real interest in machine learning. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029, and I am happy to work from the Bristol office.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience in data pipelines, experimentation and machine learning could contribute to the Food Discovery Algorithms team.",
